mated":false},"notes":[],"unFigure":{"value":34745,"what":"UN figure for 2025","date":"2025","forecast":true},"gapPct":6.8,"verdict":"un-higher","links":[{"label":"UN Statistics Division: births and deaths (table 3)","href":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/products/vitstats/seratab3.pdf"}]},{"key":"today","kind":"researched","text":"The US Census Bureau estimated Puerto Rico's population at 3,184,835 on 1 July 2025, down about 18,000 in a year and 97,000 since 2020 (reported by the Puerto Rico Institute of Statistics). The UN's figure for the same date, 3.24 million, is 1.6% higher, so they match.","figure":{"value":3184835,"what":"resident population, Census Bureau estimate (Vintage 2025)","date":"2025-07-01"},"unFigure":{"value":3235289,"what":"UN population, 1 July 2025","date":""},"gapPct":1.6,"verdict":"matches","links":[{"label":"Puerto Rico Institute of Statistics, New annual estimate of the resident population as of 2025, 12 Feb 2026","href":"https://www.estadisticas.pr.gov/en-us/blogposts/nuevo-estimado-anual-de-la-poblacion-residente-al-2025"},{"label":"US Census Bureau, U.S. Population Growth Slows..., 27 Jan 2026","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"}],"quotes":[{"text":"In summary, the total population of Puerto Rico was estimated at 3,184,835 as of July 1, 2025. This represented a reduction of around 18,000 people compared to the previous year 2024 and of about 97,000 fewer people than in 2020.","href":"https://www.estadisticas.pr.gov/en-us/blogposts/nuevo-estimado-anual-de-la-poblacion-residente-al-2025"},{"text":"Puerto Rico’s population declined by 17,686 to 3.2 million between July 2024 and July 2025, a drop of 0.6% from the prior year.","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"},{"key":"births","kind":"researched","text":"The Census Bureau counted 17,950 births and 32,857 deaths in Puerto Rico from July 2024 to June 2025. The UN expects 19,087 births in 2025, 6% more, and 34,745 deaths, also 6% more.","figure":{"value":17950,"what":"births, 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025","date":"2025"},"unFigure":{"value":19087,"what":"UN births, 2025","date":""},"gapPct":6.3,"verdict":"un-higher","links":[{"label":"US Census Bureau, U.S. Population Growth Slows..., 27 Jan 2026","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"}],"quotes":[{"text":"The main driver of Puerto Rico’s population change was negative natural change, with deaths (32,857) nearly twice as high as the number of births (17,950) between July 1, 2024, and June 30, 2025, a trend that has been consistent since 2020.","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"},{"key":"net","kind":"researched","text":"The Census Bureau estimated that 2,779 more people left Puerto Rico than arrived between July 2024 and June 2025, after a net gain of 14,425 the year before. The UN expects a net gain of 5,495 in 2025 (and 11,561 in 2024).","figure":{"value":-2779,"what":"net migration, 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025","date":"2025"},"unFigure":{"value":5495,"what":"UN net migration, 2025","date":""},"gapPct":297.7,"verdict":"un-higher","links":[{"label":"US Census Bureau, U.S. Population Growth Slows..., 27 Jan 2026","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"}],"quotes":[{"text":"The island also experienced a negative net migration of 2,779; this reversed the positive net migration (14,425) from the prior year.","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"}],"links":{"self":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries/PRI.json","countries":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries.json","risk":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/risk.json","docs":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/","site":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/country/PRI"}}
